// 400±100 ms simulated one-way (~800 ms RTT): the friend digs, the block
// must vanish from the friend's OWN world via the prediction ledger, and the
// edit must still reach the host through the lagged link. Wire-format
// details are unit-tested; this is the journey.
//
// Focus the friend's window first: unlike receiving the host's edit (network
// callbacks fire while occluded), the friend's OWN break is driven by its
// engine's rAF — which the browser throttles hard on a backgrounded page (the
// friend has sat behind the host this whole time). Occluded, its mining
// barely progresses and the prediction ledger's brief pending window can slip
// between the poll's samples; foregrounded, the engine steps at full rate.
await friend.bringToFront();
await friend.evaluate(() => {
  window.__monecraft!.net!.setSimulatedLatency(400, 100);
});

